{
  "an8.19:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 8.19 ",
  "an8.19:0.2": "2. The Great Chapter ",
  "an8.19:0.3": "With Pahārāda ",
  "an8.19:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying in Verañjā at the root of a neem tree dedicated to Naḷeru. ",
  "an8.19:1.2": "Then Pahārāda, lord of titans, went up to the Buddha, bowed, and stood to one side. The Buddha said to him, ",
  "an8.19:2.1": "“Well, Pahārāda, do the titans love the ocean?” ",
  "an8.19:2.2": "“Sir, they do indeed.” ",
  "an8.19:2.3": "“But seeing what incredible and amazing things do the titans love the ocean?” ",
  "an8.19:2.4": "“Sir, seeing eight incredible and amazing things the titans love the ocean. ",
  "an8.19:2.5": "What eight? ",
  "an8.19:2.6": "The ocean gradually slants, slopes, and inclines, with no abrupt precipice. ",
  "an8.19:2.7": "",
  "an8.19:2.8": "This is the first thing the titans love about the ocean. ",
  "an8.19:3.1": "Furthermore, the ocean is consistent and doesn’t overflow its boundaries. ",
  "an8.19:3.2": "",
  "an8.19:3.3": "This is the second thing the titans love about the ocean. ",
  "an8.19:4.1": "Furthermore, the ocean doesn’t accommodate a carcass, but quickly carries it to the shore and strands it on the beach. ",
  "an8.19:4.2": "",
  "an8.19:4.3": "This is the third thing the titans love about the ocean. ",
  "an8.19:5.1": "Furthermore, when they reach the ocean, all the great rivers—that is, ",
  "an8.19:5.2": "the Ganges, Yamunā, Aciravatī, Sarabhū, and Mahī—lose their names and c